:"https://github.com/backdrop/backdrop-issues","homepage":null,"size":211,"stargazers_count":143,"watchers_count":143,"language":null,"has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":40,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":2771,"license":null,"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":40,"open_issues":2771,"watchers":143,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"The move to standardize on YAML files for human-facing configuration files was a good idea in Drupal 8. The ability to replace a Drupal-specific format (.info files) and replace them with a readable, widely-used standard was a great enhancement.\n\nI think Backdrop should follow-suit here, but that means that we need a YAML parser as part of core. The most widely used YAML parsers are [Symfony's YAML parser](https://github.com/symfony/Yaml) and [spyc](https://github.com/mustangostang/spyc/).\n\nLicense-wise, both are options (GPL or MIT). Functionality-wise, it's kind of a coin-toss. spyc seems to be reported as faster but only supports YAML 1.0 standard. Symfony supports \"most\" of YAML 1.2.\n\nFor users moving between Drupal and Backdrop, I think adopting the Symfony YAML parser would cause the least amount of confusion. However that also means we'd need to add a PSR-0 autoloader, as is required by Symfony.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/backdrop/backdrop-issues/issues/78/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/backdrop/backdrop-issues/issues/78/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"jillro","id":301998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTk5OA